Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the limit on a chora's restarts: one that dies soon after every start is started again for good, each delay twice the last.  chora_test's [9] waits 30 s for the HAL to give crash_probe up, and the HAL never does.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --testdev --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: chora_test: \[9\] WRONG -- crash_probe on the pci-testdev at [0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: the HAL says state [12] \(given up is 3\) after [0-9]+ start\(s\), where the limit is 5
Note: the delays grow to seconds within the 30 s, so the starts it counts are few beyond the limit; that the state is not given up is what the arm reads.

